# .github/CODEOWNERS
# Mirrors FILE_OWNERSHIP.md in the format GitHub natively understands: when a
# PR touches a path below, GitHub requires review/approval from the mapped
# owner before merge. Replace the placeholder handles (@your-org/...) with
# real GitHub usernames or teams — one per pipeline stage, or one human who
# reviews on behalf of that stage while you're running this pipeline
# single-player. This is the human-facing enforcement layer; agents/_lib and
# pipeline.config.json are what a scripted CI check enforces (see
# .github/workflows/pipeline-gate.yml).

/PRD.md                        @your-org/requirements-owner
/ARCHITECTURE.md               @your-org/architecture-owner
/ARD.md                        @your-org/architecture-owner
/tests/unit/                   @your-org/test-owner
/tests/integration/            @your-org/test-owner
/tests/e2e/                    @your-org/test-owner
/src/                          @your-org/implementation-owner
/GUARDRAILS.md                 @your-org/pipeline-maintainer
/FILE_OWNERSHIP.md             @your-org/pipeline-maintainer
/ORCHESTRATION.md              @your-org/pipeline-maintainer
/pipeline.config.json          @your-org/pipeline-maintainer
/agents/_lib/                  @your-org/pipeline-maintainer
/CHANGELOG.md                  @your-org/release-owner
